By the triangle inequality $a<b+c$, $b<a+c$ and $c<a+b$, so $a-b-c<0$ while $a-b+c>0$, $a+b-c>0$ and $a+b+c>0$. Hence $\boxed{p<0}$ for every triangle.

(In fact $p=-16K^2$, where $K$ is the area of the triangle, by Heron's formula.)

