Let $a=BC$, $b=CA$, $c=AB$, let $K$ be twice the area of $ABC$, and let $O_1$ be the centre of the first circle, on $BC$. Since the circle touches $AB$ and $AC$, its radius $66$ is the distance from $O_1$ to both lines. Splitting the triangle along $AO_1$,
\[
K=2[ABO_1]+2[AO_1C]=66\,c+66\,b,\qquad\text{so}\qquad b+c=\dfrac{K}{66}.
\]

