Let $\theta=\sin^{-1}\dfrac{2}{3}$, an acute angle with $\sin\theta=\dfrac{2}{3}$. In a right triangle with hypotenuse $3$ and side $2$ opposite $\theta$, the adjacent side is $\sqrt{9-4}=\sqrt5$.

