Hence $g(12)=-10-\dfrac{15}{3}=\boxed{-15}$.

Here $AB=AC=\sqrt{65}$. All three reflections are in lines through $C$, so we work with vectors from $C$: $\vec{CA}=(-1,8)$, $\vec{CB}=(-5,1)$.

To reflect a vector $\mathbf v$ in the line through $C$ with direction $\mathbf d$, use $\mathbf v\mapsto 2\dfrac{\mathbf v\cdot\mathbf d}{\mathbf d\cdot\mathbf d}\,\mathbf d-\mathbf v$.

\textbf{Over $BC$} ($\mathbf d=(-5,1)$): $\mathbf v=(-1,8)$, $\mathbf v\cdot\mathbf d=13$, $\mathbf d\cdot\mathbf d=26$, so $\vec{CA'}=(-5,1)-(-1,8)=(-4,-7)$ and $A'=(-1,-8)$.

\textbf{Over $A'C$} ($\mathbf d=(-4,-7)$): $\mathbf v=\vec{CB}=(-5,1)$, $\mathbf v\cdot\mathbf d=13$, $\mathbf d\cdot\mathbf d=65$, so $\vec{CB'}=\dfrac{2}{5}(-4,-7)-(-5,1)=\left(\dfrac{17}{5},-\dfrac{19}{5}\right)$ and $B'=\left(\dfrac{32}{5},-\dfrac{24}{5}\right)$.

\textbf{Over $B'C$} ($\mathbf d=(17,-19)$): $\mathbf v=\vec{CA'}=(-4,-7)$, $\mathbf v\cdot\mathbf d=65$, $\mathbf d\cdot\mathbf d=650$, so $\vec{CA''}=\dfrac{1}{5}(17,-19)-(-4,-7)=\left(\dfrac{37}{5},\dfrac{16}{5}\right)$ and $A''=\left(\dfrac{52}{5},\dfrac{11}{5}\right)$.

