The slope of $AA''$ is
\[
\dfrac{\dfrac{11}{5}-7}{\dfrac{52}{5}-2}=\dfrac{-\dfrac{24}{5}}{\dfrac{42}{5}}=\boxed{-\dfrac{4}{7}}.
\]
(Check: $CA''=\sqrt{\dfrac{37^2+16^2}{25}}=\sqrt{65}=CA$, as it must be.)

Let $NC=x$. Then $AN=2x$ and $AB=3x$. Both triangles $ANC$ and $ANB$ have a right angle at $N$, so by the Pythagorean theorem
\[
AC=\sqrt{AN^2+NC^2}=\sqrt{4x^2+x^2}=\sqrt5\,x,
\qquad
BN=\sqrt{AB^2-AN^2}=\sqrt{9x^2-4x^2}=\sqrt5\,x .
\]

