$P$ and $R$ are opposite vertices, and they have the same $y$-coordinate, so the diagonal $PR$ is horizontal with length $25$. The diagonals of a rectangle are equal, so $QS=25$; its vertical component is $24$, so its horizontal component is $\sqrt{25^2-24^2}=7$. Place the centre (the common midpoint of the diagonals) at the origin: $P=(-12.5,0)$, $R=(12.5,0)$, $Q=(3.5,12)$, $S=(-3.5,-12)$.

