label("\mbox{}",(min(currentpicture,user=true)+max(currentpicture,user=true))/2,black); // keeps the text after the figure black when LaTeX typesets the labels inline
\end{asy}

With $h=2\sqrt3$ we get $s=2\sqrt3\cdot\sqrt{\dfrac{3}{2}}=3\sqrt2$. The volume is
\[
V=\dfrac{1}{3}\cdot\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}s^2\cdot h=\dfrac{1}{3}\cdot\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}\cdot18\cdot2\sqrt3=\boxed{9}.
\]

Split each polygon into isosceles triangles with two sides $1$ (radii) and apex angle $\dfrac{360^\circ}{n}$; each has area $\dfrac{1}{2}\sin\dfrac{360^\circ}{n}$:

