Put the river on the $x$-axis, the ninja at $N=(0,5)$ and the dojo at $D=(10,10)$. Reflect the dojo in the river to $D'=(10,-10)$. For any point $X$ on the river, $XD=XD'$, so the route length is $NX+XD'\ge ND'$, with equality when $X$ is on segment $ND'$:

\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(5cm);
defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));
pair Nn=(0,5),Dj=(10,10),D2=(10,-10),X=(10/3,0);
draw((-1.5,0)--(12,0),blue+linewidth(1.2));label("river",(12,0),E,blue);
